# Supply-chain hardening: disable npm lifecycle scripts (postinstall, preinstall, install)
# by default. This prevents malicious packages from executing arbitrary code during
# yarn install. See: https://www.elastic.co/security-labs/axios-one-rat-to-rule-them-all
#
# Packages that legitimately need install scripts (for native binary downloads):
#   - esbuild: postinstall downloads platform-specific binary
#   - @parcel/watcher: install compiles native addon from source
#
# After running `yarn install`, execute the allowlisted install scripts via:
#   bin/yarn-postinstall
# (which runs, for reference):
#   node node_modules/esbuild/install.js
#   node node_modules/@parcel/watcher/scripts/build-from-source.js
--install.ignore-scripts true
